      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes requested** — See inline comments for details. [[trajectory](go/traj/17fc885c-d745-43bb-b0d6-119230f066f0)]\n\n### Review Summary\n**Functionality**: Found a critical bug where `spi_flash_protect_to_reg` clears non-protection bits in the status registers (like Quad Enable), which could break SPI communication. Also identified an API compliance issue where `physical_get_protect` returns an error code instead of `1` for protected banks.\n**Style \u0026 Consistency**: Generally good. Pointed out an inconsistency where `cros_flash_rtkfp_sw_protect` does not lock mapped storage before interacting with the SPI controller, unlike other flash operations in the file.\n**Security**: The use of software write protection is implemented correctly by enforcing constraints when the physical WP pin is asserted.\n**Testing**: The CL lacks automated tests for the new driver. Please consider adding unit tests in the Zephyr test suite to cover:\n- Verification that `flash_write_prot_reg` preserves non-protection bits (`QE`, `SRPx`).\n- Edge cases in `flash_check_prot_reg` and `cros_flash_rtkfp_get_protect_flags` with different protection ranges and status register values.\n**CL Size**: The CL is small and well-scoped to adding a single new SPI flash driver and its corresponding configuration.\n\nTAG\u003dagy\nCONV\u003d803daf3d-a737-4c49-81e3-70e3dc4307fb",
