      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review]\n`spi_flash_protect_to_reg` replaces the values of `sr1` and `sr2` completely, meaning that any non-protection bits (such as `QE` for Quad Enable, `SRP0`, `SRP1`) will be lost when you write them back.\n\nYou should clear only the protection bits from the existing registers and bitwise OR the new protection bits:\n\n```c\n\tuint8_t prot_sr1, prot_sr2;\n\n\tflash_get_status(dev, \u0026sr1, \u0026sr2);\n\n\trv \u003d spi_flash_protect_to_reg(offset, bytes, \u0026prot_sr1, \u0026prot_sr2);\n\tif (rv) {\n\t\treturn rv;\n\t}\n\n\t/* Keep non-protection bits and apply new protection bits */\n\tsr1 \u003d (sr1 \u0026 ~(SPI_FLASH_SR1_SEC | SPI_FLASH_SR1_TB | SPI_FLASH_SR1_BP2 | SPI_FLASH_SR1_BP1 | SPI_FLASH_SR1_BP0)) | prot_sr1;\n\tsr2 \u003d (sr2 \u0026 ~SPI_FLASH_SR2_CMP) | prot_sr2;\n\n\treturn flash_set_status_for_prot(dev, sr1, sr2);\n```",
